<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Liberty year share soars, div up.</title>
<headline>Liberty year share soars, div up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended Dec 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr* (cts)		622.0    vs 498.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 320.0    vs 256.0</p>
<p>    Net income		13,193.5 vs 13,909.7</p>
<p>    Net premium income    7,746.4  vs 6,492.7</p>
<p>Net investment income 4,496.7  vs 3,322.7</p>
<p>    Tax			 265.7    vs 390.7</p>
<p>Net taxed operating surplus (attrib)</p>
<p>				  1,538.8  vs 1,204.1</p>
<p>Div payable April 4</p>
<p>On register March 27</p>
<p>Full name: Liberty Life Association of Africa Ltd</p>
<p>* Net taxed operating surplus per ordinary share.</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecast earnings per share on a range of 598 cents to 637 cent. A dividend increase to 320 cents from 256 cents had already been announced.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
